he FitZone, PEIF, and robust outdoor recreation programs promote\n                  physical, mental, and social health. Students benefit from a campus environment built to support\n                  success inside and outside the classroom. Community Athletics Alumni Association NMU Foundation Northern Center Continuing Education Educational Access Network (EAN) Parents Youth Programs Northern Today Events Calendar Tickets Image Northern Michigan University fosters engagement through athletics, student organizations, and a\n                  vibrant alumni network. Continuing education programs provide flexible opportunities for lifelong\n                  learning and career advancement. Together, these experiences strengthen community and extend the\n                  impact of an NMU education. Give NMU Home Apply Search NMU NMU Search Tools Search Select a Department AAUP ACADEMIC AFFAIRS & STUDENT SUCCESS ACADEMIC SENATE ADMISSIONS ALUMNI RELATIONS ANTHROPOLOGY ARCHIVES ART & DESIGN, SCHOOL OF ARTS & SCIENCES, COLLEGE OF AUDIO-VISUAL SERVICES AUDITOR, INTERNAL AUXILIARY SERVICES BEAUMIER U.P. HERITAGE CENTER BIOLOGY BOARD OF TRUSTEES, SECRETARY OF BOOKSTORE BROADCAST & AUDIO-VISUAL SERVICES BUSINESS INTELLIGENCE/INFORMATION SERVICES BUSINESS, W.L. CISLER COLLEGE OF CAMPUS RECREATION CAREER SRVCS/HIGH IMPACT LRNG CENTER FOR TEACHING & LEARNING CHARTER SCHOOLS CHEMISTRY CLINICAL SCIENCES, SCHOOL OF COMM/BROADCASTING/JOURNALISM COMMUNICATION & MEDIA STUDIES COMMUNICATIONS & PERFORMANCE STUDIES COMMUNITY AND CONNECTION, CENTER FOR COMPUTING HELPDESK CONFERENCE & CATERING SVS CONTINUING EDUCATION/WORKFORCE DEVELOPMENT CONTROLLERS OFFICE COUNSELING & CONSULTATION SERVICES CRIMINAL JUSTICE DEAN OF STUDENTS DEGREE EVALUATION DINING SERVICES-CAT TRAX DINING SERVICES-CENTRAL OFFICE DINING SERVICES-FIERAS DINING SERVICES-NORTHERN CENTER DINING SERVICES-STARBUCKS DINING SERVICES-THE LIGHTS DISABILITY SERVICES EARTH, ENVIRONMENTAL & GEOGRAPHICAL SCIENCES ECONOMICS EDUCATIO