OCIOLOGY/ANTHROPOLOGY SPEECH/LANGUAGE/HEARING SCIENCES STUDENT AFFAIRS AND SUCCESS STUDENT ENRICHMENT, CENTER FOR STUDENT LEADER FELLOWSHIP PROGRAM STUDENT SERVICE CENTER STUDENT SUCCESS STUDENT SUPPORT SERVICES SUPERIOR EDGE TECHNOLOGY & APPLIED SCIENCES, SCHOOL OF TECHNOLOGY & OCCUPATIONAL SCIENCES, COLLEGE OF TECHNOLOGY ASSET/BUSINESS MANAGEMENT TECHNOLOGY SUPPORT SERVICES TELECOM OPERATIONS THE ASSIST OFFICE THEATRE & DANCE TICKET OFFICE TICKETING, PROMOTIONS & EVENTS TITLE IX UNIVERSITY MARKETING AND COMMUNICATIONS UP NORTH FILMS UPWARD BOUND MATH & SCIENCE VENDOR PAYABLES VETERAN SERVICES WELLBEING WNMU-FM WNMU-TV A-Z Index Keyword Search Master Calendar Department Directory NMU People Search Popular Searches athletics my nmu academic calendar employment Housing Tuition human resources catalog Northern Michigan University blends strong academic programs with a vibrant sense of belonging and\n                    a welcome community, set in the heart of Michigan’s Upper Peninsula. Explore our website and see all\n                    that NMU has to offer. Home\n - Career Services \"Career Services helped me make my resume from scratch, and were always available to help me figure out what I wanted in a career. They have connected me to many different alumni that are now bringing me various professional opportunities. I would not feel as confident about my future if it were not for the help of Career Services!\" - Adeline Pavlo - '25 Social Psychology alum 93% of recent graduates who completed an internship reported that the experience helped prepare them for their career post-graduation. Search for an internship \"What started out as a simple conversation at NMU's Career Fair turned into an awesome career opportunity. Looking forward to hitting the ground running...\" -Adam Klingspon via LinkedIn - '22 Business alum Last academic year, 234 employers attended career fairs at NMU! Find YOUR next opportunity - attend an upcoming fair! Career fairs We can help you! The Career Services and High-Impact Learning office can help you with many aspects of the employment process from freshman year to senior year...and beyond! More information Fall Semester Career Fairs Professional Headshots Get your free professional headshot! Appointments are available every Friday! Schedule your appointment Welcome to Career Services and High-Impact Learning In Career Services and High-Impact Learning, it is our mission to support both students and alumni in their career development goals. We offer resources spanning from resume and cover letter development to mock interviews, job fairs, and much more! Schedule an Appointment Current students - MyNMU > Handshake, call (906) 227-2800 or chat with us - nmu.edu/careerservices Prospective students - call (906) 227-2800 or chat with us - nmu.edu/careerservices Alumni - call (906) 227-2800 or chat with us - nmu.edu/careerservices Employers - call (906) 227-2800 or email careers@nmu.edu More information Current Students Events - job fairs, employers visiting campus, professional headshot opportunities, & more. Finding a job Handshake - a platform to explore & apply for job/internship opportunities, schedule appointments, manage resumes, find career events, and more. How to log in: MyNMU > Handshake Internships On-campus job applications Resume/CV assistance See more by clicking on 'Students & Alumni' on the top menu Prospective Students Begin here - our services, FAQ, job information, job feed Events - job fairs, employers visiting campus, professional headshot opportunities, & more. Finding a job Handshake - a platform to explore & apply for job/internship opportunities, schedule appointments, manage resumes, find career events, and more. You will have access once you have attended Orientation & registered for classes. How to log in: MyNMU > Handshake. Prior to having access to Handshake, open on-campus jobs and other jobs in the U.P. can be viewed by visiting our LinkedIn . On-campus job applications Resume/CV assistance See more by clicking on 'Students & Alumni' on the top menu Alumni Alumni Relations - stay connected with NMU Career & professional development services - career services available to alumni Events - job fairs, employers visiting campus, professional headshot opportunities, & more. Handshake - a platform to explore & apply for job/internship opportunities, schedule appointments, manage resumes, find career events, and more. Log in and/or to create an account at https://nmu.joinhandshake.com/ . Mentoring - become a mentor to an NMU student Recruiting - recruit NMU students/alumni to work with you See more by clicking on 'Students & Alumni' on the top menu Employers On-campus employers: Events - see our list of upcoming events (job fairs, employers visiting campus, professional headshot opportunities, & more) FAQ - answers to questions regarding Handshake, finding employees & job fairs Handshake - a platform used to post/manage jobs & register for job fairs. Log in or create an account at https://app.joinhandshake.com . National Student Employment Week - find information & ideas on celebrating this event that takes place the second full week in April. Student employment handbook - information & resources regarding student employment See more by clicking on 'Employers' on the top menu Off-campus employers: Job Fairs - sign up for an upcoming job fair FAQ - answers to questions regarding Handshake, finding employees & job fairs Handshake - a platform used to post/manage jobs, find/message students/alumni & register for job fairs. To log in or to create an account, go to https://app.joinhandshake.com Off-Campus Federal Work-Study Program - non-profit organizations can hire students with Federal Work-study and get reimbursed for a portion of their wages. Recruiting at NMU - set up an information table, interviews, group testing, and more. See more by clicking on 'Employers' on the top menu Faculty Assignment assistance - assign a resume assignment & we will verify that students have uploaded it into Handshake Career & professional development resources - contact us with requests Classroom presentations - we can present to your class on a variety of topics Events - see our list of upcoming events (job fairs, employers visiting campus, professional headshot opportunities, & more). In conjunction with the Fall Semester Job Fair , we do host an Employer/Faculty Mixer - more information to come! Handshake - use this platform to show students what jobs (part-time, full-time, seasonal, internships) are available & help them register for a job fair & learn about upcoming events. You may also post an on-campus student job here. Job fair check-in - give credit to students that attend job fairs Resources Career resources - information on connecting with alumni & links to helpful career websites Career websites - links to career websites organized by college/major On-campus job applications See the Resource Library in Handshake for more! Upcoming Events Free Professional Headshot - September 4 Free Professional Headshot - September 11 Healthcare & Behavioral Sciences Career Fair & Health and Human Performance Employer Recruitment Event - September 14 Construction Management Career Fair - September 17 Free Professional Headshot - September 18 Free Professional Headshot - September 25 Fall Semester Job Fair - November 3 Internship Draft Day - November 4 (Lambeau Field) Engineering Technology & Occupational Sciences Career Fair - February 18 Winter Semester Job Fair - February 23 Internship Feed Business Intern - Richmond, VA at Virginia Department of Transportation - 9/4/26 Engineering Intern - Mechanicsville, VA at Virginia Department of Transportation - 9/4/26 Summer 2027 Mars Petcare Finance Internship - Science & Diagnostics at Mars, Inc. - 9/3/26 Summer 2027 Mars Snacking Operations Internship at Mars, Inc. - 9/3/26 Summer 2027 Mars Snacking Supply Chain Internship at Mars, Inc. - 9/3/26 Summer 2027 Mars Snacking Manufacturing Internship at Mars, Inc. - 9/3/26 Summer 2027 Mars Snacking Project Engineering Internship at Mars, Inc. - 9/3/26 Advisory Services Intern at Premier Inc. - 8/28/26 Graphic Design Intern - Fall 2026 at OneHope - 8/28/26 Project Coordinator (R&D) Intern - Fall 2026 at OneHope - 8/28/26 Contact NMU Career Services and High-Impact Learning Career Services and High-Impact Learning wants to help students succeed. In addition to the Handshake listings, we also offer a number of job-search workshops, job fairs, on-campus recruiting and more. Learn about all Career Services and High-Impact Learning programs and opportunities. If you've got a question - chat with us ! Look for the green tab in the lower right. careers@nmu.edu 906-227-2800 Connect with us on Social Media Facebook LinkedIn Instagram Pinterest YouTube Spotify Share your story! Facebook X LinkedIn Resources A to Z About NMU Academic Affairs Campus Map Equal Opportunity/Title IX Faculty and Staff Library Master Calendar MI Student Aid Website Mission and Vision University Marketing and Communications Careers Technology EduCat Educational Access Network (EAN) MyNMU Digital Accessibility Cookie Settings Friends Alumni Athletics Bookstore NMU Foundation Invent@NMU National Training Site Northern Today Contact Admissions Questions NMU Board of Trustees Office of the President Privacy Statement 1401 Presque Isle Marquette, MI 49855-5301 906-227-1000 NMU Torch Logo Northern Michigan University Campus Safety Logo Campus Safety Information at NMU ©2026 NMU Board of Trustees .\n      NMU is an equal opportunity institution . View accessible\n        formats for documents on this page. Northern Michigan University is located on the ancestral homelands of the Anishinaabe\n      Three Fires Confederacy. Gichi-namebini Ziibing is the traditional name of Marquette."
